.TH GIT-CLEANUP-BRANCHES 1 "2026-10-08" "Git Helpers" "git-helpers Manual"
.SH NAME
git-cleanup-branches \- delete branches that are merged into the base branch
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B git cleanup-branches
[\fB-n\fR | \fB--dry-run\fR]
[\fIbase_branch\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBgit\-cleanup\-branches\fR removes local branches that have already been merged
into a chosen base branch. If you do not specify a base branch, it lists the
available local branches and prompts you to choose one to use as the base branch.
It then walks the merged branches and asks before deleting each candidate.
.PP
When run with \fB-n\fR or \fB--dry-run\fR, it reports which branches would be
removed without deleting them.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B git cleanup-branches main
Interactively delete merged branches using \fBmain\fR as the base branch.
.TP
.B git cleanup-branches --dry-run main
Report which merged branches would be deleted without removing any of them.
.TP
.B git cleanup-branches
Prompt for the base branch, then interactively delete merged branches.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR git (1)
